  "body": "## What changed\n\nFace's posted program had no approach rapid. The facer started its path *at* its entry point in the air, so its first move was the plunge. Posts write only a move's end point, so the first posted motion after the tool call was a **3-axis feed from wherever the tool change left the spindle, straight to cutting depth** (`G01 X-5 Y5 Z-2 F100` in the old Fanuc golden).\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/face.rs`: Face starts its cursor where the other mill generators do, at (0, 0, clearance), and its first move is a rapid on the clearance plane to the entry. The plunge follows. An entry at exactly X0 Y0 (where the builder would drop a zero-length move) states the approach outright as a zero-length rapid.\n- Every dialect now posts `G00 X<entry> Y<entry> Z<clearance>` before the plunge feed.\n- The Tormach golden's old `G0 X0 Y0 / G0 Z0` opening (the #131 workaround in the script, which had no start point to use) now goes to the real entry.\n\nThe decision record is in `docs/decisions/690-face-approach.md`. A generic post-layer approach rule was considered and dropped as wider than this bug.\n\n## Goldens and tests updated\n\n- **Goldens:** the `face_square_40x40{,_blended,_stepped}.cl` goldens and all their `.nc` goldens (Fanuc, Haas, Tormach, Mazak, Sinumerik, Heidenhain) gain the approach. So do `program_entry/{fanuc,haas}_pause_home.nc`.\n- **`regression_models`:** path moves +1, posted lines +1, minutes plus the approach rapid's time.\n- **`fixture_law_gaps`:** with a clamp arm over the plunge, the gate now names the approach (move 0) as well as the plunge (move 1).\n- **`tormach_post`:** the line before the first feed is still a rapid to clearance. It now restates X Y.\n- **`machining2d`:** `rapids_only_appear_at_the_ends` and `face_steps_down_through_levels` count the approach.\n\n## Pinned by\n\n- `machining2d::rapids_only_appear_at_the_ends` (the first move is a rapid at clearance, then the plunge)\n- `machining2d::a_face_entering_at_the_origin_still_opens_with_its_approach` (new; the X0 Y0 edge)\n- the regenerated face `.cl` and `.nc` goldens (`golden_cl`, `conformance`, `fanuc_post`, `heidenhain_block_form`, `program_entry`)\n\n## How tested\n\nOn the fork base (v0.16.0):\n- all `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-motion` debug suites pass;\n- clippy on `camcraft-motion --tests` is clean.\n\nAfter merging upstream/main into the branch (an import-line conflict in `face.rs`, resolved):\n- all `camcraft-motion` suites pass;\n- every `camcraft-app` suite that uses Face passes;\n- clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nTwo failures come from upstream main and are not caused by this branch:\n- **`lathe_thread_travel` doesn't build.** This is #686.\n- **`probe_tormach` fails 6/7.** Its Tormach probe goldens from #583 are stale against #579's (#570) probe cycle. I'm filing this separately.\n\nThe other generators that start their cursor at (0, 0, clearance) may share the X0 Y0 edge. They weren't checked here; a note goes on the issue.\n\nNo machine run. The fork is synced at v0.16.0.\n\nChangelog: Face programs open with a rapid to the start point on the clearance plane instead of a feed from the tool-change position to cutting depth (#690)\n\nFixes #690\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
